Package: screenbayes
Title: Bayesian Uncertainty in Screening-Test Sensitivity and Specificity
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: 
    c(person("Vince", "Carey", email = "stvjc@channing.harvard.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
      person("Claude", "Assistant", role="ctb", comment="Most tutorial content devised agentically."))
Description: Teaching package for BST 260. Beta priors express uncertainty about
    the sensitivity and specificity of a screening test; the package computes
    posterior distributions of predictive values in target populations with
    specified prevalence, point estimates (mean, median, MAP) and interval
    estimates (equal-tailed, highest-density interval, HPD region), and ships a
    Shiny app to explore them. Students implement the components in a class
    hackathon.  rlearn tutorials are included to solidify underlying concepts.
